cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this dataset, please cite it as below, and give attribution to the
  New York Philharmonic.
type: dataset
title: New York Philharmonic Performance History
abstract: >-
  Every known performance by the New York Philharmonic and the orchestras that
  merged with it (the New York Symphony and the New/National Symphony),
  including the summer seasons at Lewisohn Stadium, from December 7, 1842 to
  today: programs, concerts, works, movements, conductors and soloists, as XML
  and JSON. Generated from the New York Philharmonic Archives' catalog and
  updated nightly; monthly releases are fixed snapshots for citation. The data
  can also be searched in the Data Explorer at https://data.nyphil.org/performance-history/.
authors:
  - name: New York Philharmonic Shelby White & Leon Levy Digital Archives
license: CC0-1.0
repository-code: https://github.com/nyphilarchive/PerformanceHistory
url: https://github.com/nyphilarchive/PerformanceHistory
keywords:
  - New York Philharmonic
  - performance history
  - concert programs
  - orchestral music
  - classical music
  - music history
  - open data
